Description: Library scans that keep the GUI responsive (DECKSMITHOS_RESPONSIVE_DB)
 A library scan adds all new tracks in a single database transaction. With
 a few thousand new files (a USB drive) the database stays write-locked for
 minutes: every GUI query (library views, sorting, settings) waits up to the
 5 s busy timeout and fails with "database is locked", the GUI is sluggish,
 settings saved on quit fail and a quit takes longer than a service stop
 timeout; an interrupted scan is rolled back completely and starts over.
 With DECKSMITHOS_RESPONSIVE_DB set:
 - the database uses the write-ahead log (PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL, kept in
   the file): readers never wait for the writer;
 - the scanner commits after every 50 tracks or 500 ms and after each
   complete directory (with its hash), announcing the tracks added so far:
   other writers wait at most for one batch, tracks appear while the scan
   runs, and a scan interrupted by a quit or a power cut resumes where it
   stopped (the directories already complete keep their hash);
 - a running scan is cancelled when the application is about to quit,
   before the windows are closed and the settings saved.
 Without the variable nothing changes.
Author: DecksmithOS
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-24
